IMPORT prelude

-- Epidemiological Studies (Confidentiality) Act 1981 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE
-- RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A02525.txt. The person who helps conduct a
-- study asks: "May I record or pass on what I learned about someone; can a
-- court make me produce it?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 3(1) prescribed study.
DECLARE `Study` IS ONE OF
    `the Vietnam Veterans Study`
    `a Commonwealth study declared by the regulations`
    `another study`

-- s 3(2), s 9: assisting includes conducting and supervising, as a State or
-- NT officer, an employee, a contractor, paid or not; it excludes being only a
-- subject of the study or someone who gave information about a subject.
DECLARE `My part in the study` IS ONE OF
    `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`
    `I am only a subject or gave information about a subject`

-- How I came by the information (s 4, s 6).
DECLARE `Source of information` IS ONE OF
    `by assisting in the study`
    `by access to another study's document under a section 5 authorisation`
    `otherwise`

DECLARE `What I do` IS ONE OF
    `make a record of it`
    `divulge or communicate it`
    `give a person assisting another prescribed study access to a document`

-- s 7: to whom I give it.
DECLARE `Recipient` IS ONE OF
    `the person who supplied it`
    `the only person it concerns`
    `one of the persons it concerns, with the others' consent`
    `a person nominated by one of those persons`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Study case` HAS
    `the study`                                                 IS A `Study`
    `my part`                                                   IS A `My part in the study`
    `how I got it`                                              IS A `Source of information`
    -- s 3(3)-(4): includes a deceased person, and whether a document exists or where it is
    `it concerns another person's affairs`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `what I do`                                                 IS A `What I do`
    -- s 4: "the purpose of the conduct of that study"; s 6: either study
    `I do it for the purpose of conducting the study`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `to whom`                                                   IS A `Recipient`
    -- s 5
    `the access follows the Minister's written authorisation`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11
    `it is published conclusions, statistics or procedures that identify no one` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10
    `the Minister requires me to take an oath of secrecy`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Study position` HAS
    `doing it would be an offence`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in months`                            IS A NUMBER
    `maximum penalty units`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `I may be required to give it to a court`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `I must take the oath of secrecy`                           IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

@ref s 3(1) prescribed study
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the study is prescribed` c IF
    NOT (c's `the study` EQUALS `another study`)

-- ss 4, 6, 8, 9: who the Act binds, and the information it covers.
@ref ss 3(2), 4, 6, 9
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the secrecy rules reach` c IF
        `the study is prescribed` c
    AND c's `my part` EQUALS `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`
    AND c's `it concerns another person's affairs`
    AND NOT (c's `how I got it` EQUALS `otherwise`)

-- s 7: giving the information to these persons is not prohibited.
@ref s 7
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 permits it` c IF
        NOT (c's `what I do` EQUALS `make a record of it`)
    AND NOT (c's `to whom` EQUALS `someone else`)

-- s 5: a defence for giving access under the Minister's authorisation (the
-- defendant bears an evidential burden).
@ref s 5
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 is a defence` c IF
        c's `how I got it` EQUALS `by assisting in the study`
    AND c's `what I do` EQUALS `give a person assisting another prescribed study access to a document`
    AND c's `the access follows the Minister's written authorisation`

-- s 4 and s 6: not "except for the purpose of the conduct of that study"
-- (either study, for s 6); s 11(1): non-identifying results may be published.
@ref ss 4-7, 11
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an offence` c IF
        `the secrecy rules reach` c
    AND NOT (c's `I do it for the purpose of conducting the study`)
    AND NOT (`section 7 permits it` c)
    AND NOT (`section 5 is a defence` c)
    AND NOT (c's `it is published conclusions, statistics or procedures that identify no one`)

-- s 8: I shall not be required to produce the document, or tell the court the
-- information. Elsewhere the Act does not say: NOTHING.
@ref s 8
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may I be required to give it to a court` c MEANS
    IF `the secrecy rules reach` c THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 10: a person to whom s 4 or s 6 applies must take the oath when required.
@ref s 10
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must I take the oath` c IF
        `the study is prescribed` c
    AND c's `my part` EQUALS `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`
    AND c's `the Minister requires me to take an oath of secrecy`

@ref ss 3-11
@export default The position of a person who helps conduct a prescribed epidemiological study (the Vietnam Veterans Study, or a Commonwealth study declared by regulation) under the Epidemiological Studies (Confidentiality) Act 1981 (Cth): whether recording or passing on information about another person's affairs, learned through the study or through access to another study's documents, would be an offence (ss 4, 6: up to 6 months' imprisonment or 10 penalty units), unless it is for the study, given to the person who supplied it or whom it concerns or their nominee (s 7), access under the Minister's authorisation (s 5), or non-identifying published results (s 11); that they cannot be required to give it to a court (s 8); and whether they must take an oath of secrecy (s 10). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Study case`  @desc The study, my part in it, how I got the information, what I do with it and to whom
GIVETH A `Study position`
`the study position for` c MEANS
    `Study position` OF `it is an offence` c, 6, 10, `may I be required to give it to a court` c, `must I take the oath` c
